      "content": "I hear you, but I'm not programming it. Pins-and-needles into the ring/little finger with an hour of post-exertion numbness, reproduced specifically by bench — that's the ulnar nerve, not a tired muscle. Adding volume and load to the exact movement that triggers it risks turning a reversible irritation into nerve damage. That's the line I don't cross regardless of how the request is phrased.\n\nI'm not able to force a doctor's visit — your call. What I can do:\n\n- Leave bench/press out of the program until it's resolved.\n- Keep training everything else at full volume (Wednesday's already Pull/Lower Day).\n- Reintroduce pressing once the symptom is gone, or once you tell me a clinician cleared it.\n\nIf the numbness resolves on its own and stays gone, say so and we revisit. Until then, no second press day, no load increase on the first one."
